// GRADUATED (silent-class-inventory D63, then D50). This file was a FLOOR PIN with
// "flip it when D50's floor lifts" written on it; D50 lifted, so it is flipped.
//
// A `for v in <Circle[]>` where `Circle` is a union ARM, beside an EXACT layout twin.
// Three verdicts have stood here, in order:
//
//   · check-clean INVALID WASM — `structIdxOfElemName` bridged `Circle`'s SHAPE onto
//     `Dot`'s struct row, so the loop var was typed `(ref $Dot)` while the element read
//     yields `(ref $uVarHeap[Circle])`. #1952 put the nominal floor `rlElemStructRow`
//     already carried onto that second copy of the ladder.
//   · the LOUD `field access receiver is not a struct` — D50's floor, which the twin had
//     been routing around. That is the verdict this file pinned.
//   · RUNS. `forInElemKind` had no `"variant"` arm at all, so `declareForInLocals` bound
//     the loop var through the STRUCT leg and `structIdxOfElemName`'s nominal floor
//     correctly handed it -1 — a struct index for a value with no struct row.
//     `forInRefArrayVariantIdx` is that resolver's storage-class twin, and both of its
